From 9b85c0d05905b4ecd120c5e31d6403b909af35eb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 15:23:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] perf(roster): gate owner reads on input and store generation
 [daveey]

Roster only needs membership, not complete session payloads or token flushes.
Repeated polls hydrated system prompts/tool schemas for every live work owner
and discovered route namespaces even when all owners had authoritative stored
ids. Gate those reads on their actual inputs and committed connection generation;
keep registry enumeration, scope and execution-observation clocks fresh.

Memo is per SessionDB object/actual connection, invalidated by total_changes,
data_version, namespace changes and new owner candidates. Pending transactions
are uncached so rollback cannot preserve an uncommitted answer. Entries retain
only current keys. Narrow get_session_list_row avoids the unrelated payload path.

RED: full hydration assertion and 3-vs-1 owner-resolution count both fail on
original handler. GREEN: 41 focused tests, then 9 invalidation and 51 admission
consumer tests passed; scripts/check all 20 checks OK. Due-time expiry, activity,
generation, process exit, ownership, namespace, external commit, replacement DB,
rollback and write-during-read covered.

Synthetic 467-call nonempty K=2/8/32 replay (distinct live PIDs, real SessionDB,
210KB prompt per owner): CPU 1.249852->0.430085s, 1.833212->0.314934s,
3.298628->0.497315s. Component profiles retained separately; no assertion of
historical K, deployment or combined whole-rpc acceptance. Parent J owns the
unchanged <=1% whole-row gate; no serve lifecycle/workload changes performed.
